### Step 3 - Test against the null hypothesis (CA)

We are now able to conduct an F-test to compare the 2 models :

```{r FtestCASA, warning=F, message=F}
LL0 <- LogLikelihood_CA    # log-vraisemblance du modèle CA
LL1 <- LogLikelihood_SA    # log-vraisemblance du modèle SA

p0 <- 0         # nombre de paramètres additionnels dans le modèle CA (par rapport à ta base)
p1 <- 1         # un paramètre d'interaction dans le modèle SA

D <- 2 * (LL1 - LL0)
p_val <- pchisq(D, df = p1 - p0, lower.tail = FALSE)

cat("Comparison CA/SA - D =", D, "p =", p_val, "\n")

```

The SA model is not significatively different than the CA model. There is no significant interaction between EPX & IMD for cocoon production. Therefore, the best model to represent the data is the CA model.

